# Layout, comments, quoting style and numeric spelling are all invisible to
# the hash, and none of them needed a special case — the vendored atom table
# compares unescaped values and integer digits, so `"x" == 'x'` and
# `1_000 == 1000` fall out of the same mechanism that makes heredocs work.
#
# `Gamma#render` is the boundary: a different string *value* is a different
# method. Normalization removes spelling, not meaning.
#
# It is also where the two tiers visibly do different jobs on one input. The
# exact tier keeps Gamma out, because the literal really did change. The near
# tier reports it, because the shape is otherwise identical — which is exactly
# the judgement a person wants when deciding whether two methods are worth
# merging. Only one near pair appears rather than two, because Alpha and Beta
# share a normalized body and a near pair is about *shapes*, not call sites.
dupes  Alpha#render+Beta#render  Alpha#render+Gamma#render
